-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Move Step Mid To Target
-- statement:
--   **Self-consistency moves the third slice effect to the right register.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, let $\zeta$ be an error parameter, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Assume that the left and right completed slice measurements are $\operatorname{SDDRel}$-related under the uniform slice-question distribution with error
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{sc}}=2\zeta.
--   $$
--
--   For three slice questions and an $r$-tuple of tail points, the mid family places all three distinguished slice effects on the left and the reversed tail half-product on the right. The target family keeps the first two effects on the left, while placing the reversed tail half-product followed by the third slice effect on the right. Then
--
--   Write $\mathcal Q$ for the finite set of slice questions. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q^3\times\mathbb{F}_q^r)}
--   \!\left(\mathcal M_r^{\mathrm{mid}},\mathcal M_r^{\mathrm{target}};E_{\mathrm{sc}}\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the single move estimate used to advance the half-sandwich commutation chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_moveStepMid_toTarget`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
